1_data_prep/test_lc/

# compute_landcover.py's raw ESA WorldCover tile downloads -- always
# written to <--out-dir>/wc_tiles/ regardless of what --out-dir is (see
# download_tiles()'s out_dir / "wc_tiles" call), so this catches it even
# when --out-dir isn't the default ./wc (which the "wc" entry above only
# catches by coincidence). Each tile is 50-100+ MB and GitHub rejects
# pushes with files over 100MB outright -- these are a re-downloadable
# cache (compute_landcover.py re-fetches anything missing), never meant
# to be committed.
wc_tiles/
*.tif

# sail train/validate configs are fully reconstructible from
# pipeline_configs/state_registry.yml + generate_train_config.py /
# generate_validate_config.py -- not worth versioning each run (matches
# sail's own configs/ being gitignored). geoetl download configs ARE
# tracked (configs/geoetl/) -- they're a record of what was actually
# downloaded, matching geoetl's own configs/tlags/ convention. Generated
# SLURM job files (both under configs/geoetl/ and configs/sail/) aren't
# tracked either way -- regenerate any time from the config + generator.
configs/sail/
configs/**/*.sh
*slurm*
